# About the Contributor(s)

**Restu Bias Primandhika** is a lecturer whose expertise includes
language learning, linguistics, and digital learning media. He received
his master's degree in Indonesian Language Education from IKIP
Siliwangi and is currently a doctoral student at Universitas
Muhammadiyah Prof. Dr. Hamka. Since 2018, he has served as a lecturer
in the Faculty of Language Education at IKIP Siliwangi. He has written
several papers on the impact of learning technology on cognitive
abilities, including studies on digital media preferences among
Indonesian language education students, lecturers' pedagogical
responses to AI's impact on students' oral presentation skills, and an
experiment on an Indonesian-to-Sundanese transformer-based neural
machine translation model with Sundanese speech-level evaluation. His
research interests include digital learning media, Indonesian language
education, learning technology, pedagogical innovation, artificial
intelligence in education, and machine translation. He can be contacted
at <restubiasprimandhika@uhamka.ac.id>. ORCID ID:
<https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9715-8530>

